      {
        "id": "com-sn-4",
        "name": "Samoussa aux Poissons (Fish Samosas)",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "servings": 12,
        "prepTime": 30,
        "cookTime": 15,
        "ingredients": [
          "Filling: 300g fresh tuna or bonito (flaked), onion, garlic, ginger, chili, cilantro, lemon juice",
          "Wrappers: spring roll sheets or homemade dough (flour, water, oil)",
          "Oil for deep frying",
          "Hot chili sauce for dipping"
        ],
        "instructions": [
          "Cook fish with onion, garlic, ginger until flaked and dry",
          "Season with chili, cilantro, lemon juice — filling must be intense",
          "Let filling cool completely",
          "Cut wrappers into strips, fold into triangles, fill, seal with water paste",
          "Deep fry at 170°C until golden and crispy — 3-4 min",
          "Drain well",
          "Serve hot with chili sauce",
          "In Moroni, samoussa vendors line the streets at dusk during Ramadan — the fragrance is the advertisement"
        ],
        "description": "Comorian fish samosas — fresh tuna wrapped in crispy pastry, a fusion of Indian and African traditions on these volcanic islands. The Ramadan evening samoussa rush in Moroni, when every neighborhood has vendors frying hundreds at once, has become a viral scene of Indian Ocean food culture."
      }
